Status: NOT_STARTED - deferred backlog; do not begin without a new request.
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/79
Milestone: Select a boxed GBA or NDS game on the desk and play its ROM.
Dependencies: 79 for NDS loading; GBA library work is independent of79.
Bundled ROMs and artwork require title-specific redistribution permission.

Purpose:
Place GBA and NDS game boxes on the table, with their cartridges inside.
Selecting a box should load its corresponding game into the appropriate
console without making the user provide the ROM on every play session.
Keep the option to load the user's own ROMs.

Tasks:
- [ ] Establish the game catalogue and ROM/box-art provenance and permissions.
      Workstream61's media-only clearance is not blanket permission for new
      titles, runtime testing or integration.
- [ ] Model the GBA/NDS boxes and their contained, system-appropriate
      cartridges on the table.
- [ ] Make boxes selectable by mouse and touch, with clear game/system
      identification and accessible equivalent selection.
- [ ] Map each box to its authorized ROM, load it through the existing
      cartridge flow into the correct console and surface download errors.
- [ ] Preserve per-game/per-system saves, switching behavior and user-ROM
      upload; include only explicitly cleared catalogue assets in delivery.
- [ ] Verify actual box-to-ROM gameplay, repeat selection without a file
      picker, save isolation and unavailable-asset handling; update docs.

Acceptance criteria:
The table contains both GBA and NDS boxed cartridges. Selecting a game box
loads that exact game's ROM into the matching console without requesting a
local ROM each time. Switching titles does not overwrite unrelated saves.
User-uploaded ROMs remain supported and private files are never bundled.
Only redistribution-cleared games/artwork ship; catalogue failures are
visible and do not claim a game has loaded.

Completion evidence:
None. No games or artwork have been selected, downloaded, executed or
bundled; no boxes, catalogue, loading integration or tests have been started.

Completion log:
2026-11-06: Owner requests selectable boxed GBA/NDS cartridges and automatic
ROM loading as future work only. Record the dependency on79 for the DS
portion without unnecessarily blocking the independent GBA portion.
